{title: The Comforter Has Come}
{artist: Frank Bottome / William J. Kirkpatrick}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Opening}
{key: C}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{score: the-comforter-has-come.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (The_Comforter_Has_Come-The_Comforter_Has_Come) and the Cyber Hymnal score (100% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]O spread the tidings ’round,
[C]Wher[F]ever man is found,
[F]Wher[C]ever human hearts
[C]And [Am]human [D7]woes a[G7]bound;
[G7]Let [C7]every Christian tongue
[C7]Pro[F]claim the joyful sound:
[F]The [C]Comforter__[G7]__ has [C]come!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]The Comforter has come,
[C]The [F]Comforter has come!
[F]The [C]Holy Ghost from Heav’n,
[C]The [Am]Father’s [D7]promise [G7]giv’n;
[G7]O [C7]spread the tidings ’round,
[C7]Wher[F]ever man is found—
[F]The [C]Comforter__[G7]__ has [C]come!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]The long, long night is past;
[C]The [F]morning breaks at last;
[F]And [C]hushed the dreadful wail
[C]And [Am]fury [D7]of the [G7]blast,
[G7]As [C7]o’er the golden hills
[C7]The [F]day advances fast!
[F]The [C]Comforter__[G7]__ has [C]come!__[F]__[C]__[Am]__[D7]__[G7]__[C7]__[F]__[C]__[G7]__[C]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Lo, the great King of kings,
[C]With [F]healing in His wings,
[F]To [C]every captive soul
[C]A [Am]full de[D7]liverance [G7]brings;
[G7]And [C7]through the vacant cells
[C7]The [F]song of triumph rings:
[F]The [C]Comforter__[G7]__ has [C]come!__[F]__[C]__[Am]__[D7]__[G7]__[C7]__[F]__[C]__[G7]__[C]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]O boundless love divine!
[C]How [F]shall this tongue of mine
[F]To [C]wondering mortals tell
[C]The [Am]matchless [D7]grace di[G7]vine—
[G7]That [C7]I, a child of sin,
[C7]Should [F]in His image shine!
[F]The [C]Comforter__[G7]__ has [C]come!__[F]__[C]__[Am]__[D7]__[G7]__[C7]__[F]__[C]__[G7]__[C]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]Sing, till the echoes fly
[C]A[F]bove the vaulted sky,
[F]And [C]all the saints above
[C]To [Am]all be[D7]low re[G7]ply,
[G7]In [C7]strains of endless love,
[C7]The [F]song that ne’er will die:
[F]The [C]Comforter__[G7]__ has [C]come!__[F]__[C]__[Am]__[D7]__[G7]__[C7]__[F]__[C]__[G7]__[C]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
